<article id="thinking-tools-guide" class="mcp-page">
  <header class="border-b border-stone-300 bg-white">
    <div class="mcp-shell py-10 sm:py-12">
      <p class="mcp-eyebrow">A guide to thinking with RationalGrid</p>
      <h1 class="mcp-title mt-5 max-w-3xl">What would help you understand?</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
        Choose what you need below. Each direction offers one tool to start with, an example to try and other options when you need them.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Not sure where to start?
        <.tool_link id="thinking-tools-start" tool="explain" class="font-semibold text-teal-800">
          Try explaining the idea in your own words.
        </.tool_link>
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <div class="mcp-shell max-w-4xl py-8 sm:py-10">
    <div id="thinking-goals" role="group" class="space-y-3" aria-label="Choose a thinking goal">
      <details
        :for={group <- @tool_groups}
        id={group.id}
        name="thinking-goal"
        data-thinking-goal
        class="thinking-guide-group"
      >
        <summary id={"thinking-goals-#{group.id}"} class="thinking-guide-summary">
          <h2 class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 items-center gap-4">
            <span class="mcp-icon-tile" aria-hidden="true">
              <.icon name={group.icon} class="h-5 w-5" />
            </span>
            <span class="min-w-0 flex-1">
              <span class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold sm:text-2xl">{group.title}</span>
              <span class="mt-1 block text-sm font-normal leading-6 text-slate-600">
                {group.question}
              </span>
            </span>
            <.icon
              name="hero-chevron-down"
              class="thinking-guide-chevron h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-teal-800"
            />
          </h2>
        </summary>
        <div class="border-t border-stone-200 px-5 pb-5 sm:px-6 sm:pb-6">
          <p class="py-4 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">{group.description}</p>
          <%= for {tool, index} <- Enum.with_index(group.tools) do %>
            <p
              :if={index == 1}
              class="mb-2 mt-6 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500"
            >
              Other ways to explore this question
            </p>
            <article
              id={tool.key}
              data-thinking-tool
              tabindex="-1"
              class={[
                "thinking-guide-tool",
                if(index == 0,
                  do: "border border-teal-800/20 bg-[#edf3ef] px-4 sm:px-5",
                  else: "border-b border-stone-200"
                )
              ]}
            >
              <details
                id={"thinking-example-#{tool.key}"}
                name={"thinking-tools-#{group.id}"}
                open={index == 0}
                class="thinking-guide-tool-disclosure"
              >
                <summary class="thinking-guide-summary px-0 py-4 sm:px-0">
                  <h3 class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 items-center gap-4 font-semibold">
                    <span class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                      <span
                        :if={index == 0}
                        class="mb-1 block text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-800"
                      >
                        A place to start
                      </span>
                      {tool.label}
                    </span>
                    <.icon
                      name="hero-chevron-down"
                      class="thinking-guide-chevron h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-teal-800"
                    />
                  </h3>
                </summary>
                <div class="space-y-4 pb-5 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
                  <p>{tool.help}</p>
                  <div class="border-l-2 border-teal-700 pl-4">
                    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-800">
                      Try asking
                    </p>
                    <blockquote class="mt-2 font-serif text-lg leading-7 text-slate-950">
                      {tool.example}
                    </blockquote>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-slate-800">What to look for in the result</p>
                    <p class="mt-1">{tool.insight}</p>
                  </div>
                  <p :if={Map.get(tool, :availability)} class="text-xs leading-6">
                    {tool.availability}
                  </p>
                </div>
              </details>
            </article>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
    <section class="mt-8 border-t border-stone-300 pt-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold">One useful step can be enough.</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Read the result before choosing another tool. What is clearer? What still needs checking? Stop when you have something useful.
      </p>
      <details id="using-thinking-tools" class="mcp-disclosure mt-4">
        <summary class="min-h-11 cursor-pointer py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-teal-800">
          How to use these tools in the app or with an AI assistant
        </summary>
        <div class="grid gap-6 pb-4 pt-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold">In a RationalGrid grid</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
              Open <strong>Show thinking tools</strong>
              beneath the response form, or select a passage to work on that exact point. Available tools depend on your selection and editing access.
            </p>
            <.link
              id="thinking-tools-app-guide"
              href={~p"/intro/how#guide-critical-thinking-tools"}
              class="mcp-text-link mt-2"
            >
              Read the app guide
            </.link>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold">With your AI assistant</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">
              Name the idea or passage and ask in ordinary language. Your connected assistant can use a tool and read its result before choosing another step.
            </p>
            <.link
              id="thinking-tools-assistants"
              href={~p"/features/ai-assistants"}
              class="mcp-text-link mt-2"
            >
              Connect an AI assistant
            </.link>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-xs leading-6 text-slate-600">
        AI-generated arguments and source suggestions need your judgement. Check important claims against their sources, and distinguish facts, interpretations and hypothetical cases.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</article>
